      "enabled": true
    },
    {
      "comment": "The REAL vault, the material dp-gnosis actually serves — every other entry is an English proxy. `derive` projects the ingested atoms plus the hand-authored golden set into the BEIR layout at `source` on EVERY run: both inputs are local files this repo already carries, so there is nothing to fetch and a cache could only measure a vault that has since changed. The atom FILENAME is the document id, which is what `relevantAtomIds` names and what `score.ts` recovers from `originPaths`.",
      "id": "vault",
      "format": "beir-local",
      "qrels": "test",
      "source": "data/vault",
      "derive": {
        "atoms": "../../dp-gnosis/vault",
        "golden": "../dp-gnosis/golden/golden-set.v2.json"
      },
      "domain": "project-vault",
      "docShape": "atom",
      "queryShape": "keyword-and-question",
      "enabled": true
    },
    {
      "comment": "The Hungarian half of the same material, against its own golden set. Read it WITH the printed unreachable-gold count: 22 of its 117 judgments name atoms this corpus does not hold, so its recall is bounded well below 1 and its numbers are NOT comparable with `vault`.",
      "id": "vault-hu",
      "format": "beir-local",
      "qrels": "test",
      "source": "data/vault-hu",
      "derive": {
        "atoms": "../../dp-gnosis/cache/atoms-hu",
        "golden": "../dp-gnosis/golden/golden-set-hu.v1.json"
      },
      "domain": "project-vault-hu",
      "docShape": "atom",
      "queryShape": "hungarian-question",
      "enabled": true
    }
  ]
